          "text": "**2026-10-19** — From S03 (2026-10-19): an idle daemon unlinks its socket before releasing the pidfile lock, so a start racing that exit gets ErrAlreadyRunning; treat it as transient and reuse App.connect's StartWait (internal/cli/cli.go:175-195) instead of a second 5 s wait. Package-level cli.Run has no Start function; S13 builds an App with Start.",
          "created_at": "2026-10-19T04:08:54Z",
          "attempt": 0,
          "by": "Jon R",
          "verified_by": "",
          "verified_at": "",
          "stale_after": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "c5856cf8-4d56-428f-b387-4c3ff692aaf3",
          "kind": "",
          "text": "**2026-10-19** — From S15 (2026-10-19): Cache.Forget does not cancel in-flight reads, and a snapshot or status that loaded the registry before projects rm can re-create the forgotten project's entries (handlers.go:281, cache.go:139). Notices go out one connection at a time from the cache's read goroutine (subscribe.go), so a stuck subscriber delays others up to the 10 s write timeout. With no subscriber every project is still read every 30 s until idle exit. ork status text shows no part ages (JSON does). Open records follow the 5 s / 30 s tick, as the integration review's R2 table has it.",
